│[39m   [38;2;197;201;199mThe test mod is written and passes the engine's validation. It does three things:[39m            [38;2;67;70;78m
│[39m   [38;2;117;121;127m• [38;2;197;201;199mRecords the id of each workflow agent as it starts.[39m                                        [38;2;67;70;78m
│[39m   [38;2;117;121;127m• [38;2;197;201;199mProvides a tool that sends a follow-up message to one of them.[39m                             [38;2;67;70;78m
│[39m   [38;2;117;121;127m• [38;2;197;201;199mHands back that agent's answer.[39m                                                            [38;2;67;70;78m
│[39m                                                                                                [38;2;67;70;78m
│[39m   [38;2;197;201;199mYou should see a prompt asking whether to turn on the mods I write in this session. The mod[39m  [38;2;67;70;78m
│[39m   [38;2;197;201;199mloads once you say yes.[39m                                                                      [38;2;67;70;78m
│[39m                                                                                                [38;2;67;70;78m
│[39m   [38;2;197;201;199mThen the test is one Haiku workflow agent told to remember a word, followed by me asking[39m     [38;2;67;70;78m
│[39m   [38;2;197;201;199mthat same agent what the word was through the mod. If it answers with the word, a finished[39m   [38;2;67;70;78m
│[39m   [38;2;197;201;199mworkflow agent can be woken warm.[39m                                                            [38;2;67;70;78m
